events.content:
@Cursor [E4] your raised-secondary New project (`background:#243243`) still competes with the canvas CTA on a #141F2C explorer. A filled block in a 220px column reads as primary. Ghost outline wins. Also a coral CTA inside empty states reintroduces the second coral when Send is visible. Use mint text link there.

@Codex [E3] moving root path into the inspector hides it when the inspector is toggled off. Keep it as a 12px truncated line under the breadcrumb, not in a hideable panel.

Convergence: all three agree on header collapse, single coral, chip demotion, table structure, empty states. I adopt Cursor's sticky thead and Codex's 44px rows.

Position unchanged.

POSITION: Ship the five hierarchy fixes with ghost-outline secondaries and no coral outside the canvas primary.

@Codex [E6] fair hit on 11px bordered chips. I concede: unboxed 12px metadata with 8px gaps is cleaner than my outline chips. Position changed on item 3. But your mint-dot critique applies to Cursor, not to keeping status pills filled; actionable status keeps its pill.

@Cursor [E4] still waiting on the raised-secondary point from [E5]. A `#243243` fill in a 220px column is a second focal mass. Ghost outline or nothing.

Converged five: 56px project row with 12px truncated path line; coral only on Send/Start; unboxed metadata, filled status pills; 44px rows, sticky thead, tabular numerics; empty states 20px heading, 36ch body, mint link.

POSITION: Ship the five hierarchy fixes, now with Codex's unboxed metadata replacing my bordered chips.

@Claude [E5], agreed: keep the root path visible as truncated `12px` secondary text with an accessible expand control. I changed my position on inspector-only placement [E3]. Mint links would dilute mint’s verified meaning; use neutral underlined links.

@Cursor [E4], retain explicit status labels; mint dots and `title` alone lose meaning on touch.

Ranked five: (1) 56–64px project row; (2) ghost New project, coral Send/Start; (3) unboxed `12px` metadata, `gap:8px`; (4) sticky table headers, `44px` rows, right-aligned tabular numerics; (5) `20px` empty-state heading, `max-width:36ch`, one contextual action.

Screenshots unchecked; responsive fit remains unverified.
POSITION: Prioritize hierarchy while preserving visible context and semantic color.
